<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Engineered by uncoalesced -->
<!--
  Android 11 and below. `data_extraction_rules.xml` carries the same intent for Android 12+;
  the platform reads one or the other by version, never both, so any rule added there has to be
  mirrored here or it applies to only some of the install base. minSdk is 26, so this covers
  real devices rather than being a formality.

  READ THIS BEFORE ADDING AN `exclude` HERE. This format does not work like the Android 12+
  one. As soon as a single `include` is present, the system backs up *only* what is included
  and everything else is excluded already. An `exclude` for a path that was never included is
  not defence-in-depth, it is a no-op, and `lint` fails the build on it (FullBackupContent)
  precisely because writing one usually means the author believed the opposite.

  So the protection here is the shape of the list itself: `keyboard_database` - the learned
  personal dictionary and the clipboard history - is absent, and absence is what keeps it off
  Google's servers. Same for the sticker index, the sticker bytes and the background images,
  which are omitted to stay far below the 25MB cloud quota. Passing that quota does not
  degrade gracefully: the OS stops backing the app up at all and keeps serving a stale
  snapshot without telling the user.

  One thing this format cannot express: there is no `disableIfNoEncryptionCapabilities` here,
  it is Android 12+ only. On a pre-12 device with no lock screen the backup is not
  end-to-end encrypted and no manifest attribute refuses it. Keeping the sensitive data out of
  the list is the only defence available on those versions, which makes this list matter more
  there, not less.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <!-- Settings, themes and layouts. Small, and the things a user is annoyed to lose. -->
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="keyboard_preferences.xml" />
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="app_preferences.xml" />
    <include domain="file" path="themes/" />
    <include domain="file" path="layouts/" />
</full-backup-content>
